WEBVTT

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:03.100
Can we make Nino a guitarist and vocalist?

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:04.140
Rejected.

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:05.770
It's missing something.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:08.010
<i>Better!</i>

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:13.570
Don't attack with technique. 
Attack with emotion.

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:16.160
Even if you do go berserk, we'll be there.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.780
Throw more of how you feel 
into it than you ever have.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:22.010
Once I made the lyrics into my own words,

00:00:22.010 --> 00:00:25.250
I felt like I truly sang for the first time.

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.250
You said you were writing a new song, right?

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:30.840
The lyrics...

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.040
Can I try writing them?

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:45.040
Look! The new In NO Hurry album is out.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:45.980
Really?!

00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:48.730
I've been looking forward to this.

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:49.990
I'm gonna buy it.

00:00:49.990 --> 00:00:52.710
She's buying it! I want to give her a hug!

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:52.200
Hey!

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:53.990
You'll get arrested!

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.990
Whatever the case, it's a relief 
that the album's been released.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.750
Yuzu-kun, texting?

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:03.530
Yeah. I'm telling Alice about 
the girl who bought our album.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:07.590
What's Ninocchi been up to? She's been 
going straight home from school lately.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.130
She's writing lyrics for our new song.

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:11.080
What?!

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:13.050
I haven't given her the OK yet, though.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:15.130
Why not? Sounds good to me.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:19.450
Because obviously any lyrics she 
writes are going to be about Momo.

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:21.480
I don't want to hear anything like that.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.480
I know what you mean. 
Our poor king of underdogs!

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:27.930
What kind of nickname is that?!

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:29.830
We came up with it yesterday!

00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:31.440
Well, that's a new one!

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:35.560
But this will be a change of pace, 
and isn't that more fun?

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:39.450
Nino can't just stay trapped 
in your cage forever.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:43.220
And above all, it'll be easier for her to

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:45.330
put her feelings into it 
if it's her own words.

00:01:45.330 --> 00:01:47.010
I know that!

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:47.710
But...

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:50.330
When she's singing is the only time she's...

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:52.520
I know what you mean! Exactly!

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.960
Our poor great king of underdogs!

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.520
So now I'm upgraded to a great king?!

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:58.930
Do your best, emperor of underdogs!

00:01:58.930 --> 00:01:59.800
Emperor?!

00:02:02.860 --> 00:02:05.980
Writing lyrics is so hard!

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:41.990
♭11 I'll Make It So All of Them Can Never Leave

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:44.970
In the bath at night, I set the 
bath temperature to 40 degrees.

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:48.730
What's the matter, Miou? 
Your face looks dead.

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:52.830
Why am I listening to such a weird 
song on my summer break?

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:55.190
Composition: Yuzu. Lyrics: Nino.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:57.420
Huh? You're writing lyrics? That's amazing.

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:00.190
I just said I wanted to write them.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:02.800
He said he'd decide whether 
to use them after hearing them.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:08.900
I think I can sing even louder if I can 
sing songs I put into my own words.

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:10.810
It's a battle with my computer every day.

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:14.410
So you can sing even louder by 
singing, "My bath's 40 degrees"?

00:04:14.410 --> 00:04:16.900
No. It feels completely out of place.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.820
Then don't make me listen.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:22.000
Why don't you just write about Momo?

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:26.260
I-I kind of feel embarrassed 
to write about Momo.

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:28.580
I can if it's all insults, though.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.380
Seriously? What a waste.

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:33.080
And you're singing at the same festival.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:44.340
That crappy band.

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:57.720
Nino-chan's working in the music 
industry now, too, isn't she?

00:04:58.860 --> 00:05:01.280
Have you grown taller again?

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:05.530
It's been a while, Momo.

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:09.410
Mom...

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:13.620
Do you live around here now?

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.360
No.

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:16.920
How about Nino-chan?

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.190
Does she still live in Hase?

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:19.080
She doesn't.

00:05:19.620 --> 00:05:21.680
Nino isn't in Kamakura anymore.

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:23.340
She moved to Tokyo.

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:25.060
I see.

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:27.320
Later.

00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:32.850
Nino-chan's selling very well, too, isn't she?

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:35.600
I'm glad I saw you.

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:38.290
I'll come back again.

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.110
Momo

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:45.360
Momo 

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.170
<i>I can't!</i>

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:50.040
<i>It's way too embarrassing to put 
what I'm feeling into words!</i>

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:52.180
<i>Lyricists must all be masochists!</i>

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:59.980
<i>The new song is more intense 
than all his other songs.</i>

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:02.540
<i>The melody's more emotional 
than any before.</i>

00:06:04.040 --> 00:06:05.380
<i>It feels good.</i>

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:09.160
<i>I wonder how Yuzu usually writes lyrics.</i>

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:11.760
<i>Does he ever get embarrassed?</i>

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:15.690
<i>He wrote "Canary" about me.</i>

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:17.770
That's it!

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:18.660
Yuzu!

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:28.180
It's the "Canary" demo.

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:34.260
I heard this on a commercial just now.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:36.660
Kanade, you wrote this, didn't you?

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.230
No, you're wrong! There's no way—

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:40.790
I'm not wrong.

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:46.060
This vocalist, "Alice"... Are you still forcing 
that poor girl to be your substitute?

00:06:46.810 --> 00:06:49.300
Just set her free already!

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:53.370
I'm sure she regrets it.

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:55.670
I'm sure she wishes she'd never met you.

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:58.180
Don't make me repeat myself!

00:06:58.180 --> 00:06:59.810
Get rid of music!

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:02.290
Music kills people!

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:11.240
Mom, Dad didn't die because of music.

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:15.210
Shut your mouth!

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:17.080
You're crazy.

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:22.420
I'm not crazy.

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:22.420
August 12
Appearing in Rock Horizon!!

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:25.750
Let me stay here!

00:07:26.010 --> 00:07:28.110
Huh? Hey!

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:35.140
You're here early. Rock Horizon 
is the day after tomorrow.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:38.270
I know that! Just let me stay here.

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:40.020
I can't take any more.

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:42.460
What happened?

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:43.940
Stuff.

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:46.500
That doesn't tell me anything.

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:48.400
Hey, Yana...

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.030
I think I might be crazy.

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:57.050
Does Alice regret... meeting me?

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:59.420
I have no idea what you're talking about.

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:03.670
Anyway, about Nino being both a guitarist 
and vocalist... I think it's still too soon.

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:10.520
Yuzu,

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:13.440
I'm on your side, okay?

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:23.060
Set List 
1. Canary 
2. Wednesday Beauty 
3. New Song (temp) 
4. Borderline 
5. High School

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:25.020
All right, rehearsal's done.

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:27.340
So tomorrow's the day!

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:29.990
Is this set list really okay?

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:31.820
It's fine, it's fine.

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:33.150
U-Um...

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:35.410
I wrote lyrics for the new song.

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:37.790
Can we try it before we leave?

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:40.290
It's here! Let's do it!

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:42.280
Can you play the guitar with it?

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:43.790
I'll manage.

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:46.960
Then let's do it after a five-minute break.

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:47.960
Sure.

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.570
I can't wait!

00:08:51.570 --> 00:08:52.590
Here.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:53.890
Thanks.

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:56.300
Are you okay with doing the new song?

00:08:56.540 --> 00:08:57.530
Whatever.

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:04.200
All right, we'll have a go at the new song.

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:04.890
Let's do it!

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:05.480
Right!

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:32.840
<i>We're hiding how we truly feel</i>

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:38.220
<i>Your lips touch my throat while your 
voice turns to foam and disappears</i>

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:44.180
<i>Ever since that day, on the other 
side of your sound is where</i>

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:45.780
<i>My voice will always be</i>

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:47.750
<i>I found it, and I'm sending it</i>

00:09:46.120 --> 00:09:49.290
She can sing like this?

00:09:47.750 --> 00:09:50.060
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:54.530
She's overflowing with passion like usual,
but somehow, it's gentle.

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:54.530
<i>I'm standing in front of a whirlpool 
with only a song in my hand</i>

00:09:56.510 --> 00:10:00.340
<i>This is the only weapon I have</i>

00:10:00.340 --> 00:10:02.070
<i>Now, let's dance</i>

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:04.950
On the other side of your sound is where 
my voice will always be

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:03.770
<i>Wait...</i>

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:08.290
While your voice turns to foam 
and disappears

00:10:05.780 --> 00:10:07.120
<i>This isn't about Momo.</i>

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:11.290
Your lips touch my
throat

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:09.590
<i>It's about...</i>

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:13.920
I've missed you 
all this time

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:13.000
<i>me.</i>

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:17.760
I'm happy I met you

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:16.400
<i>It's about me.</i>

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:21.460
<i>If I resound what's in my heart</i>

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:23.470
<i>It will reach</i>

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:27.230
<i>to you</i>

00:10:40.630 --> 00:10:41.530
Pass!

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:44.270
We're leaving in an hour.

00:10:44.270 --> 00:10:45.870
Now get ready to go.

00:10:47.350 --> 00:10:49.780
We did it!

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:55.170
Hey.

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:58.820
Those lyrics... Why did 
you write them about me?

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:02.770
I tried writing them about me, Momo, and you,

00:11:02.770 --> 00:11:05.680
but I could only finish them
when they were about you.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:08.870
Maybe because you're 
the person closest to me.

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:12.060
We're even similar in how we 
struggle with who we like.

00:11:13.090 --> 00:11:15.480
Speaking of, who's the person you like, anyway?

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:19.600
Who do you think?

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:21.950
Take a guess.

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:25.050
I don't have a clue!

00:11:25.050 --> 00:11:26.700
That's what I thought!

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:30.080
Did you think of a title for that song?

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:31.560
You're going to use it?

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:34.460
Well, the crappy quality 
gave it a good flavor.

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:36.900
Let's see.

00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:40.450
It's a big jumble of different feelings, so...

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:44.110
How about "Noise"?

00:11:57.190 --> 00:11:59.190
<i>The top Japanese music festival,</i>

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:01.120
<i>Rock Horizon,</i>

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:05.610
<i>begins now.</i>

00:12:06.610 --> 00:12:08.880
<i>Starting this year, there are four stages.</i>

00:12:08.880 --> 00:12:10.970
<i>The 30,000-capacity Horizon Stage.</i>

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:14.460
<i>The 10,000-capacity Sunset Stage.</i>

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:17.460
<i>The 8,000-capacity Ground Stage.</i>

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:20.550
So this is where the black cats will be.

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:21.570
It's big.

00:12:22.230 --> 00:12:23.220
<i>And...</i>

00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:25.860
<i>The stage where In NO Hurry will play,</i>

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:28.100
<i>the 5,000-capacity Flight Stage.</i>

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:32.640
Hmm...

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:35.850
"A cheap band at the top of the charts."

00:12:36.050 --> 00:12:38.050
"In NO Hurry rip-off."

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:39.230
"Annoying."

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:44.240
"In NO Hurry sells on looks alone."

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:46.870
"It has no place in a music festival."

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:49.120
The black cats? They'll just humiliate 
themselves in the best time slot! 

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:49.120
They write whatever they want.

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.620
Come on, a masked band? lol
They'll be gone by next year.

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:51.620
These guys don't have a clue.

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:54.370
They're underestimating us.

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:57.380
You're the ones who are going to be wiped out.

00:12:59.910 --> 00:13:01.130
This is bad.

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:01.880
Huh?

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:04.050
The guests are starting to move.

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:05.920
What do you mean?

00:13:05.920 --> 00:13:08.060
The festival has several different stages,

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:12.140
so if people get bored with a band's 
performance, they'll leave right away.

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:15.640
Apparently, it's super visible 
from up on the stage.

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:18.870
While you're performing, you can see 
the crowd get smaller and smaller!

00:13:19.420 --> 00:13:20.580
Pretty scary!

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:24.060
I wonder if I'll be able to 
stop people from leaving.

00:13:25.050 --> 00:13:26.660
That doesn't matter.

00:13:27.330 --> 00:13:30.900
We get to play on this huge stage.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:32.890
Let's crush it.

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:35.500
<i>Our sound.</i>

00:13:36.410 --> 00:13:37.620
<i>That's right.</i>

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:39.500
<i>I'm not alone.</i>

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:42.820
<i>Everything that's happened 
since that day culminates here.</i>

00:13:43.990 --> 00:13:45.980
<i>This stage is just the beginning for us!</i>

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:49.250
<i>Momo's here today, too.</i>

00:13:50.340 --> 00:13:51.560
<i>I'll make my sound resound.</i>

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:54.660
<i>Deeper than the scratch on Momo's guitar.</i>

00:13:54.660 --> 00:13:56.170
<i>Enough to shake him.</i>

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:00.230
Nino has nothing to do with this!

00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:02.430
Damn it.

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:04.160
Kiryuu-kun?

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:08.990
Hey! Where are you going?

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:10.560
Kiryuu-kun!

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:17.080
Talking 
Mother

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:16.040
Come back home. Aren't we family?

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:18.750
Damn it.

00:14:19.180 --> 00:14:20.630
If you do...

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:23.960
I won't do anything to Nino-chan.

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:29.090
Set List 

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:28.440
<i>I'm starting to get really nervous.</i>

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:30.770
<i>It's finally time.</i>

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:34.680
<i>Right about now, I'm sure Momo and his 
band are on standby at their stage, too.</i>

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:47.180
Momo?

00:14:50.150 --> 00:14:52.920
Wh-What? Isn't it almost your turn?

00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:54.120
I can make it if I run.

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:57.410
Nino, lend me your head.

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:03.590
It won't be like six years ago.

00:15:04.150 --> 00:15:05.760
I don't want to just leave

00:15:06.230 --> 00:15:07.720
without saying anything.

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:11.570
<i>Huh? Wait, what did he just...</i>

00:15:13.030 --> 00:15:13.700
Nino,

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:16.100
this time is for real.

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:18.620
Goodbye.

00:15:27.530 --> 00:15:28.410
<i>Momo...</i>

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:30.990
<i>Wait.</i>

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:32.630
<i>Momo.</i>

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:34.450
<i>Momo!</i>

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:35.910
Alice.

00:15:36.980 --> 00:15:39.380
It's about time. Hurry.

00:15:46.740 --> 00:15:47.940
<i>I have to go after him.</i>

00:15:49.140 --> 00:15:52.590
<i>He can't leave when I still 
haven't told him I lied.</i>

00:15:53.400 --> 00:15:54.850
<i>I have to go after him.</i>

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:55.990
<i>I have to tell him.</i>

00:15:56.550 --> 00:15:58.400
<i>That I still like him.</i>

00:15:58.400 --> 00:16:00.100
<i>That I love him.</i>

00:16:00.550 --> 00:16:01.600
<i>I have to tell him.</i>

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:05.110
<i>I have to tell him. I have to tell him. 
I have to tell him. I have to—</i>

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:06.230
Alice.

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:06.230
Ninocchi.

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:06.230
Nino.

00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:15.450
You're twenty minutes late, Alice.

00:16:15.690 --> 00:16:17.200
I don't mind teaching you.

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:19.160
Welcome to In NO Hurry.

00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:22.750
Man, that seriously felt amazing!

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:25.500
Can we make Nino a guitarist and vocalist?

00:16:25.890 --> 00:16:28.750
Throw more of how you feel into 
it than you ever have, Alice.

00:16:28.950 --> 00:16:32.450
We get to play on this huge stage.

00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:36.960
<i>I am Alice.</i>

00:16:38.200 --> 00:16:39.250
I'm going.

00:16:40.820 --> 00:16:42.140
I have to sing.

00:16:43.470 --> 00:16:44.830
<i>The concert is starting.</i>

00:16:46.640 --> 00:16:48.290
You two better be prepared.

00:16:49.410 --> 00:16:52.650
Alice is probably going 
to go super berserk today.

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:55.270
Perfect!

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:07.420
We've got a great audience here.

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:12.420
<i>Momo's stage is about one 
kilometer away from here.</i>

00:17:12.950 --> 00:17:13.700
Nino.

00:17:14.890 --> 00:17:16.550
If we can't see each other anymore...

00:17:17.260 --> 00:17:19.880
I hope, one day, we can 
use your song as a guide

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:21.290
to find each other again.

00:17:22.550 --> 00:17:23.930
<i>I will make my sound resound.</i>

00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:27.370
It's time. All right, give it your all!

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:28.440
Right!

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:30.390
<i>With this voice,</i>

00:17:33.080 --> 00:17:34.450
<i>I'll stop you.</i>

00:17:39.010 --> 00:17:41.950
<i>Yeah, I can see them well.</i>

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:45.460
<i>All the fans, directly in front of me.</i>

00:17:46.010 --> 00:17:48.280
<i>Most of the people farther behind them</i>

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:50.210
<i>are here out of curiosity.</i>

00:18:09.490 --> 00:18:10.860
<i>She's starting with "Noise"?</i>

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:12.110
<i>But the set list...</i>

00:18:12.110 --> 00:18:13.550
<i>She's completely ignoring it?!</i>

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:32.250
<i>We're hiding how we truly feel</i>

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:33.150
A new song?!

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:37.550
<i>Your lips touch my throat while your 
voice turns to foam and disappears</i>

00:18:33.150 --> 00:18:34.250
Sweet!

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:43.310
<i>Ever since that day, on the other 
side of your sound is where</i>

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:44.560
<i>My voice will always be</i>

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:44.560
<i>Alice.</i>

00:18:44.930 --> 00:18:46.960
<i>I found it, and I'm sending it</i>

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:48.550
<i>Is it even harder to put the brakes 
on because you wrote the lyrics?</i>

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:49.050
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

00:18:50.050 --> 00:18:51.380
<i>And really...</i>

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:53.780
<i>I'm standing in front of a whirlpool 
with only a song in my hand</i>

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:54.570
<i>Didn't you write this song about me? 
Don't sing it to him!</i>

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:59.150
<i>This is the only weapon I have</i>

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:00.910
<i>Now, let's dance</i>

00:19:00.910 --> 00:19:03.990
<i>Around and around, 
tumbling as we dance and spin</i>

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:05.800
<i>On top of sound</i>

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:08.750
<i>Crossing, sounding, singing</i>

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:11.430
<i>Where the sound of the sand ends up</i>

00:19:12.040 --> 00:19:15.080
<i>Around and around, revolving, 
you spin your tale</i>

00:19:15.080 --> 00:19:17.300
<i>Toward a crucible of sound</i>

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:20.130
<i>This is a song to reach you</i>

00:19:20.440 --> 00:19:22.140
<i>Hey, listen</i>

00:19:23.100 --> 00:19:25.930
<i>I've missed you all this time</i>

00:19:26.150 --> 00:19:28.700
<i>I'm so happy we met</i>

00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:31.400
<i>I've missed you, I've missed you</i>

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:34.020
<i>I'm so happy we met</i>

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:37.200
<i>Let's put an end to the 
days where we fight alone</i>

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:39.780
<i>And grab hold of the 
sound overflowing from us</i>

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:41.080
<i>You and me</i>

00:19:41.750 --> 00:19:45.200
<i>Let's smile together</i>

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:48.370
<i>Our goal is far, and we 
can only barely see it</i>

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:50.450
<i>Like the moonlight</i>

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:50.450
<i>Momo.</i>

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:53.190
<i>Let's hold hands and stamp our feet</i>

00:19:53.190 --> 00:19:55.850
<i>Toward that light</i>

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:55.620
<i>Momo.</i>

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:59.470
<i>Gently, with our cobbled-together music</i>

00:19:59.470 --> 00:20:01.770
<i>Sealing it with a kiss</i>

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:01.220
<i>Momo!</i>

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:04.850
<i>If you're here with me</i>

00:20:05.030 --> 00:20:06.850
<i>I can keep going</i>

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:10.570
<i>Around and around, 
tumbling as we dance and spin</i>

00:20:10.570 --> 00:20:12.510
<i>On top of sound</i>

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:15.270
<i>Crossing, sounding, singing</i>

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:18.000
<i>Where the sound of the sand ends up</i>

00:20:18.560 --> 00:20:21.680
<i>Around and around revolving, never ending</i>

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:23.860
<i>Toward a crucible of sound</i>

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:26.910
<i>If I resound what's in my heart</i>

00:20:25.710 --> 00:20:26.660
<i>Momo.</i>

00:20:27.210 --> 00:20:29.030
<i>It will reach out</i>

00:20:29.030 --> 00:20:30.210
<i>I won't let you leave!</i>

00:20:29.030 --> 00:20:34.060
<i>To you</i>

00:20:53.280 --> 00:20:54.620
<i>Not just Momo.</i>

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:57.230
<i>I'll make it so</i>

00:20:58.200 --> 00:21:00.150
<i>all of them can never leave.</i>

00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:06.990
♭12 I Pray It Reaches You

00:21:09.180 --> 00:21:12.500
<i>The girl who lives next door to me, 
Nino, almost never smiles.</i>

00:21:15.410 --> 00:21:17.000
Momo, let's sing.

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:20.590
What should we sing today?

00:21:20.790 --> 00:21:23.590
<i>She only smiles when she sings with me.</i>

00:21:24.210 --> 00:21:26.810
The stars are pretty, so 
"Twinkle, Twinkle, Little Star."

00:21:26.810 --> 00:21:29.120
I was thinking the same thing!

00:21:29.530 --> 00:21:30.990
One, two!

00:21:30.990 --> 00:21:35.770
<i>Twinkle, twinkle, little star</i>

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:40.230
<i>How I wonder what you are</i>

00:21:40.570 --> 00:21:45.220
<i>Up above the world so high</i>

00:21:40.620 --> 00:21:45.230
<i>At night, if I open my window and sing 
my heart out while looking at the moon,</i>

00:21:45.220 --> 00:21:50.120
<i>Like a diamond in the sky</i>

00:21:45.230 --> 00:21:48.490
<i>I can no longer hear the sounds 
of the huge fights that happen</i>

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:49.900
<i>downstairs every night.</i>

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:54.870
<i>Twinkle, twinkle little star</i>

00:21:51.410 --> 00:21:54.410
<i>And Nino, who sings with her 
mouth wide open like a fool,</i>

00:21:54.870 --> 00:21:59.680
<i>How I wonder what you are</i>

00:21:55.640 --> 00:21:56.870
<i>is really,</i>

00:21:58.250 --> 00:21:59.370
<i>really...</i>

00:22:01.770 --> 00:22:03.930
If the suit suits you—

00:22:02.980 --> 00:22:04.670
Oh, my mom's here.

00:22:05.360 --> 00:22:06.850
Goodnight, Momo!

00:22:07.430 --> 00:22:08.540
Yeah.

00:22:09.510 --> 00:22:13.390
Pun book

00:22:10.710 --> 00:22:13.390
<i>I've always thought about a certain thing.</i>

00:22:13.990 --> 00:22:16.560
<i>I put all my effort into 
making puns every night.</i>

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:18.020
<i>And she ignored it again.</i>

00:22:19.090 --> 00:22:20.300
<i>Tomorrow for sure.</i>

00:22:21.070 --> 00:22:23.120
<i>Tomorrow for sure, I'll make her laugh.</i>

00:22:24.500 --> 00:22:25.570
<i>All right.</i>

00:22:25.570 --> 00:22:29.150
<i>I stayed up all night making this one. 
It's my best work yet.</i>

00:22:34.870 --> 00:22:37.730
And it was super fun!

00:22:39.950 --> 00:22:43.380
Look at that. She can laugh.

00:22:49.870 --> 00:22:50.760
Momo!

00:22:51.270 --> 00:22:54.390
You meanie! How could you leave without me?

00:22:56.470 --> 00:22:59.850
What were you talking about with that guy?

00:22:59.850 --> 00:23:02.500
Nothing at all.

00:23:02.500 --> 00:23:03.730
I see.

00:23:03.730 --> 00:23:06.280
Are you mad? Why?

00:23:07.550 --> 00:23:09.890
<i>I was only talking about you...</i>

00:23:11.500 --> 00:23:14.280
Because you were laughing, and it looked cute.

00:23:15.350 --> 00:23:18.820
<i>I wanted to be the only one to see her smile.</i>

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:21.780
<i>Whatever!</i>

00:23:21.780 --> 00:23:24.040
<i>I'm done making puns as of today!</i>

00:23:24.260 --> 00:23:27.510
The apple fell into ap-pool!

00:23:39.380 --> 00:23:42.130
<i>He thinks I'm cute! Cute!</i>

00:23:42.130 --> 00:23:44.190
<i>That's the first time he's said that to me.</i>

00:23:44.790 --> 00:23:46.940
<i>Maybe I'm a genius when it comes to puns.</i>
